#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129198 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129016 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "d3ae6c85-14bd-57ad-b8cc-1cebb53683b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-7346" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/8} \\int_0^{\\sin2\\theta} r \\, \\textrm d r\\,\\textrm d \\theta.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{[{r}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the double-angle formula\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} = 1-2\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin^22\\theta = \\dfrac12\\left(1-\\cos4\\theta\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(0-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{2}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(\\pi -2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561310 :question-generator/id #uuid "43d838a8-510b-5e27-b55a-fa4325567ad2" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129198.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129626 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7aa44b-cefc-5820-8f30-d5e2344ef950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321243} {:answer/id #uuid "296bd36f-2f4a-5195-8d23-67afa8466ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321469} {:answer/id #uuid "5994704b-000c-507d-a814-14894c25981b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321854} {:answer/id #uuid "663ac189-5c11-5931-88ff-1f3a097d9de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321939} {:answer/id #uuid "eacb236a-ca73-5bff-8d2f-ea5761a80a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eacb236a-ca73-5bff-8d2f-ea5761a80a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322985} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f3bb291-72e9-573f-8060-c17a7f541fdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fcddcef-1856-5848-a572-712ca0d53c78" :question/math-academy-id "q-38031" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,[{r}^{2}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acba3f29-0158-52f0-9456-91c5be61af4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127268} {:answer/id #uuid "b65a27eb-39be-5bb5-a399-1d44b7927674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127269} {:answer/id #uuid "dacc8225-ad29-548c-99c4-034d05c1b2ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127270} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a0d310-0000-5652-8ada-f073e31a559d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127271} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc4c481-03e9-5e2b-b660-a09ea114f9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127272}] :answer-field/id #uuid "74727eb8-963c-5008-8d8c-d65c40ef415d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127267}] :question/id #uuid "4de8b5f4-2e7e-535e-81ad-97991889d6bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-38127" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{π/3}^{π/2}\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}r^{2}\\sin θdrdθ$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a78120fd-44f8-51c1-b9dd-5784c7ddde90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276989} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf96883-ff35-5cf9-b8c9-ef1449820eff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277149} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b7cf35-e4e8-5645-988c-d9decc7eb447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277218} {:answer/id #uuid "d256a689-9115-5115-b8cc-dca87fe713d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277332} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b78b6c-d3db-508c-85cc-e0ca239ccf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3b7cf35-e4e8-5645-988c-d9decc7eb447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277218} :answer-field/id #uuid "2939712c-1519-5b89-99ce-fbfcd86f2f1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aff73867-9b1f-5562-9960-420de4061c93" :question/math-academy-id "q-161049" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{sin}^{3}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\frac{1}{3}{sin}^{3}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(1-\\frac{1}{3})-0] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59029508-b3c4-5856-9e82-8be13d20dfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321849} {:answer/id #uuid "5bfe432d-69ae-5f45-8501-b2941dd6da47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321875} {:answer/id #uuid "73b5e790-d197-591e-8023-1b42b9c19647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322050} {:answer/id #uuid "84f4df8e-914d-5611-8d98-3e64db0593e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322199} {:answer/id #uuid "a8213e0d-3524-56f9-9f0b-d587a6a113bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bfe432d-69ae-5f45-8501-b2941dd6da47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321875} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8f76a21-833b-5523-ac04-4ad00b86b928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7818e95-0cd3-5ca9-8225-4d2224300f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38133" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17565734-926b-52e3-8121-3fbdaea7f5fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348644} {:answer/id #uuid "4509f43f-e1e1-5642-b552-7ac3e8a361a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349073} {:answer/id #uuid "5b19110d-ad5e-5ffa-9e28-33a3151ac8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349285} {:answer/id #uuid "670fa60a-c544-5a09-9fe7-cd3fdc72ce28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349391} {:answer/id #uuid "908f282c-0775-5149-a41c-32c4e538f86a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b19110d-ad5e-5ffa-9e28-33a3151ac8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349285} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f1e2bf0-e7fe-5f40-96b3-f24b49a5f589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06a556db-bf08-5756-8218-a6278b5b6e16" :question/math-academy-id "q-83511" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({3}^{4}-{1}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =20{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =20[\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2}]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =10{[{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =10({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{sin}^{2}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =10(1-0) \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "766cc68a-3d23-5f16-ba87-3f8f5800b901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352609} {:answer/id #uuid "77d5fbd2-7c92-549f-93b3-1fdc63f38113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352616} {:answer/id #uuid "a2097643-cd6a-574e-9d94-468a5f04b054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352954} {:answer/id #uuid "a485bba6-e236-5258-93a5-a3bb1a8603c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352972} {:answer/id #uuid "ef83d9b5-3baa-586b-9c44-1971f5324b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef83d9b5-3baa-586b-9c44-1971f5324b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353652} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe41175-b766-5595-800a-8ed923d6727b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1bcf047-04fc-54ad-9345-94ccc9c748a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-83957" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =6[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431388eb-9598-575f-ad76-d3f33ee209fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352183} {:answer/id #uuid "44f3a20a-620f-5a8c-955b-ae48e7b8cd59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352204} {:answer/id #uuid "ae068552-f076-510a-8dee-4a77718965b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353042} {:answer/id #uuid "bd34ba33-c031-5097-a731-809dc1c41e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8-\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353178} {:answer/id #uuid "cc455a3f-3a88-5672-92b6-a2ec611e8f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd34ba33-c031-5097-a731-809dc1c41e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8-\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353178} :answer-field/id #uuid "43682371-f791-5e91-a473-d5d5a1fad81e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38812bca-4749-5693-ba84-2da96d03ab77" :question/math-academy-id "q-83958" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({1}^{2}-(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\theta -\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{8-\\pi }{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea2ccdb-2b2b-5e06-a8bd-a29481af05f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430733} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7ef1ee-27c1-50f3-af3d-a2b63e2d03d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430738} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3e76f1-42b1-5f3d-8b32-cf741baa2a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430740} {:answer/id #uuid "5e28ab03-180e-5b20-af37-557e7db4d91e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430743} {:answer/id #uuid "77346f94-7bc7-5551-a9ff-5850737d6c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ea2ccdb-2b2b-5e06-a8bd-a29481af05f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430733} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ca73348-922c-58d8-8087-d4874ab8f01d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c4c9c61-2471-5bbd-bac4-3d2dcc4d6268" :question/math-academy-id "q-83514" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2}2r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2}2r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}[{r}^{2}]_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({2}^{2}-{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(4-{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(4-{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =[4\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ]_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =(2\\pi +0)-(\\pi +1) \\\\  & =\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cf5461b-da0e-570c-b9aa-467a2f82071d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430741} {:answer/id #uuid "5d101e08-dd8a-5f3e-96a5-138bde512f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430742} {:answer/id #uuid "681f0aba-b493-51e6-a417-42799a6f3a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430744} {:answer/id #uuid "73fa4118-327c-5da0-ace4-6324c8542c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430748} {:answer/id #uuid "e5117ec4-182c-58a0-848d-ff0ac8238d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73fa4118-327c-5da0-ace4-6324c8542c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430748} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a4db397-2205-5620-8d4c-677784accd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "414bd17b-1eab-5df7-bb84-eb1080abae7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161048" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}5{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}5{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}5{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta [{r}^{5}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(-1-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40fcf753-0267-53ac-aa07-33aca198c3c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430737} {:answer/id #uuid "566fc95d-9cf1-5eeb-ae90-c8f8a3969e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430739} {:answer/id #uuid "686056c3-1712-5837-8d5c-57ad9de19f24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430745} {:answer/id #uuid "a84ffeca-f3ff-5817-85cf-b80c75007d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430752} {:answer/id #uuid "e43ffd51-6f41-504e-a3ea-d2e5f89becd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "566fc95d-9cf1-5eeb-ae90-c8f8a3969e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430739} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9a63565-3b3e-5f4e-ac3a-4fbb44e6e16d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9231aa24-53fe-5011-80b7-3b4b62ca8c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-83966" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{1}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]_{1}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ((2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-{1}^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{4}{3}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]}_{5\\pi /3}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(-\\frac{4}{3}{cos}^{3}⁡(2\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi ))-(-\\frac{4}{3}{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)-(-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f095421-4eb7-5ea2-bb40-6f8eab7c9244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561270} {:answer/id #uuid "50e6ac1d-86b6-55d3-8bb3-54ede029e824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561284} {:answer/id #uuid "9f55bc3e-6963-5fa2-a551-7d6fe2d56a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{6} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561295} {:answer/id #uuid "bac92365-b494-5840-afdc-098f66ee52c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561299} {:answer/id #uuid "d37d1246-b0a1-5b46-966a-737ac55ada39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d37d1246-b0a1-5b46-966a-737ac55ada39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561302} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca07c4a4-cf13-5b88-93c7-0238e693af51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2c6baa40-7c4d-5d92-bf70-a91f0dc92cbe" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 2 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 2 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2 \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2 \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2 \\left(\\frac{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the double-angle formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(2x)=2\\cos^2 x-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(2\\theta\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = 2\\left[\\theta + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} \\\\\n& = 2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)+\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13dfb5ec-6677-5544-a923-1388141c6808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{12} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561271} {:answer/id #uuid "41db61bc-7623-5367-81d4-b14e7b7a0c29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{16} + \\frac{\\p