ituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(2\\theta\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 1\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = 1\\left[\\theta + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} \\\\\n& = 1\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 1\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 1\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)+\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Expressed in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "386dc02b-9808-5e39-9f81-54316d3f3422" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{496 \\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561275} {:answer/id #uuid "54595002-c5f5-53bb-9648-7ea78fc7201f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 30 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561287} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad68cc9-50aa-5747-8835-4f69180b5014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561289} {:answer/id #uuid "9ddb7d20-54d5-575e-bbb4-c342ec45763d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561294} {:answer/id #uuid "bfef2e39-597